/**
	A list of the names of all sound input devices, such as microphones, available on the system.
	const string[]@ sound_input_devices;
	## Remarks:
		The index of a device in this array is the device number accepted by the `microphone` constructor. Passing -1 instead of an index selects the system's default input device.
		The array may be empty if the system has no input devices. Each read asks the system for its devices anew, so a device plugged in or removed while the program runs shows up the next time you read this property. An array you already hold doesn't change, so its indexes stay those of the list as it was when you read it; when the system can't list its devices, a read gives the last list it gave. Asking the system takes a moment, so keep the array rather than reading the property again for every element. The array can't be modified; make a copy first if you want to change it, for example to build a menu.
		Reading this property starts the sound system if it hasn't been started yet.
*/

// Example:
void main() {
	const string[]@ devices = sound_input_devices;
	if (devices.length() == 0) {
		alert("Input devices", "No input devices were found.");
		return;
	}
	alert("Input devices", "The following input devices are available: " + join(devices, ", "));
}
